Subject to the restrictions in section 4 and to your compliance with
this Licence, the Author grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide,
royalty-free, non-transferable and non-sublicensable licence to:

2.1  USE. Install and run the Software, for any purpose, on any number
     of computers and game accounts, free of charge.

2.2  MODIFY FOR YOURSELF. Modify your own copy of the Software in any
     way, for your own use only. WoW addons ship as readable Lua, every
     user already has the full source on disk, and forbidding people to
     edit their own files would be both pointless and hostile. A copy
     you modified remains subject to section 4.

2.3  STUDY. Read the source, study how it works, and apply what you
     learned in your own code written by you. Ideas, techniques and
     approaches are not claimed by this Licence; the expression of them
     in the Software's code is.

2.4  QUOTE. Quote any part of the Software in a bug report, a forum
     post, a review, a tutorial or any other discussion of the
     Software, provided the quotation is no longer than the discussion
     reasonably requires and the Software is identified as its source.

2.5  WRITE A MODULE. Write an addon of your own against the module
     contract the Software declares - the global object created by
     Core/Api.lua, which ships with every copy - and distribute that
     addon under terms of your own. A module is your work, not a
     Derived Work: it calls the contract rather than incorporating the
     Software's code. Quoting the contract's own examples is covered by
     section 2.4.

     This grant stands on the contract as the Software declares it, not
     on any document describing it. The Author's written contract is
     published separately and may be asked for at the address in
     section 13; its absence from a copy of the Software takes nothing
     away from this permission.

