6. THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES
================================================================================

6.1  The Software uses libraries written by other people. They are
     shipped under Libs/ as unmodified copies, they are not part of the
     Software as defined in section 1.1, and nothing in this Licence
     applies to them: each is redistributed under its own terms, which
     this Licence neither replaces nor restricts.

6.2  Those libraries are:

     - Ace3 (AceAddon-3.0, AceEvent-3.0, AceConsole-3.0, AceDB-3.0,
       AceDBOptions-3.0, AceGUI-3.0, AceConfig-3.0,
       CallbackHandler-1.0) - the Ace3 licence, a BSD-style permissive
       licence. https://github.com/WoWUIDev/Ace3

     - LibSharedMedia-3.0 by Elkano - LGPL v2.1.
       https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/libsharedmedia-3-0

     - LibStub - placed in the public domain by its authors.

6.3  Each library keeps whatever copyright and licence notices its own
     files carry, and section 4.5 protects those notices as it protects
     the Author's.

6.4  LibSharedMedia-3.0 is shipped as plain, unmodified Lua source, so
     anyone holding a copy of the Software can replace or modify that
     library, as the LGPL requires. The restrictions in section 4 do
     not apply to it.

6.5  Libs/ is not kept in the Author's repository; tools/fetch-libs.ps1
     fetches it, and tools/package.ps1 includes it in the release
     archive.

6.6  LibDataBroker displays are read from whatever addons publish them.
     No such addon is bundled with the Software, and none is required
     by it.

6.7  Everything else the Software ships is the Author's own work. Its
     status bar textures and branding images are generated by the
     Python tools under tools/ from code in this repository.

